IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `rtw-dates`
IMPORT `rtw-core`

-- Return to Work Act 2014 (SA), with the Return to Work Regulations 2015 -- the employer's questions.
--
-- SEAT: the employer of an injured worker (the pre-injury employer in s 18), a small business or a company. The text
-- puts real duties on this party: send ReturnToWorkSA a copy of a notice of injury and forward a claim within 5 business
-- days (ss 16(6), 30(5); maximum penalty $1 500 each), furnish the information it reasonably requires (s 30(6)), provide
-- suitable work (s 18) and answer a worker's subsection (3) notice within 1 month (s 18(4b)), and give 28 days notice
-- before ending an injured worker's employment (s 20). A self-insured employer is outside ss 16(6), 30(5) and 30(6); its
-- delegated functions as compensating authority (s 134) are not encoded. The questions are worded "Must I ...?", "By when
-- must I ...?", "Is this person my worker?". The rules are in rtw-core.l4; this module restates none. Its names differ from
-- the worker seat's (rtw-seat.l4), so a case file can import both and assert mirror cases.
--
-- BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Return to Work Act 2014 (SA) -- the employer's questions`

§§ `Who is my worker (s 4, regs 5 and 6; s 7)`

@export Is this person my worker under the Return to Work Act 2014 (SA) (s 4(1), (2); regs 5 and 6)?
GIVEN `I employ this person` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you employ this person under a contract of employment
      `this person is my apprentice or trainee` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person works for you under a contract of apprenticeship, including as a trainee
      `I pay this person while giving on-the-job training` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you give this person on-the-job training in a trade or vocation and pay them during it
      `the kind of work they do for me` IS A `Prescribed class of work` @desc Whether the work is one of the kinds the regulations bring in (reg 5): building work other than tiling, window cleaning, other cleaning, driving under a local government award, taxi driving without the licence, driving or riding a non-commercial vehicle to deliver goods, entertaining at a venue, thoroughbred riding as a licensed jockey, award outwork, or the work of a minister or member of a religious order; otherwise none of them
      `the work is for my trade or business` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the work is done in the course of, or for the purposes of, a trade or business you carry on
      `they do the work personally` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person does the work themselves
      `they employ someone to do part of it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person employs anyone else to do part of the work
      `the materials they supply are worth` IS A NUMBER @desc The value in dollars of the materials this person supplies, or is expected to supply (0 if none)
      `the whole job pays them` IS A NUMBER @desc The total in dollars payable to this person under the arrangement (only matters for building work)
      `their most valuable tool is worth` IS A NUMBER @desc The price in dollars of a new equivalent of their most valuable tool or item of plant or equipment (only matters for building work)
      `the arrangement lasts this many months` IS A NUMBER @desc How many months the arrangement runs for (only matters for cleaning; 1 for a month or less)
      `they run more than 1 vehicle for work at once` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person owns or operates more than one vehicle for work at the same time (only matters for delivery work)
      `the goods are or were theirs or mine` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the goods carried are, or were ever, owned by this person or by you (only matters for delivery work)
      `I or someone related supply their vehicle` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you, or someone related to you, own, lease, hire out or otherwise supply the vehicle this person drives (only matters for an owner-driver of a commercial vehicle)
      `they are fishing crew paid by a share` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person is crew on your fishing boat paid by a share of its profits or gross receipts
      `they are a volunteer of a prescribed class` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether this person is a volunteer of whom the Crown is the presumptive employer (Act Schedule 1)
      `the Corporation has extended cover to them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ReturnToWorkSA has extended the Act's protection to this person as a self-employed worker (s 175)
      `their regulation 6 class` IS A `Regulation 6 class` @desc Whether this person is in a class the regulations exclude (reg 6): a minister, priest, pastor or deaconess named in reg 6(1); a contestant employed for a sporting or athletic activity (but not a licensed race rider or driver, or a boxer or wrestler engaged for a fee); a driver carrying goods in a commercial motor vehicle they own, lease or hire; a person covered by the Seafarers Rehabilitation and Compensation Act 1992; otherwise none
      `the CPI for the latest September quarter` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of last year
      `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014` IS A NUMBER @desc The Consumer Price Index (All groups, Adelaide) for the September quarter of 2014
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this person my worker` IF
    `the person is a worker`
        (`Engagement facts` WITH
            `employed by the other person`                                             IS `I employ this person`
            `an apprentice or trainee under a contract of apprenticeship`              IS `this person is my apprentice or trainee`
            `paid while receiving on-the-job training in a trade or vocation from the other person` IS `I pay this person while giving on-the-job training`
            `the class of work`                                                        IS `the kind of work they do for me`
            `the work is done for the purposes of the other person's trade or business` IS `the work is for my trade or business`
            `the work is done personally`                                              IS `they do the work personally`
            `someone else is employed to do part of the work`                          IS `they employ someone to do part of it`
            `the value of the materials supplied`                                      IS `the materials they supply are worth`
            `the total payable under the arrangement`                                  IS `the whole job pays them`
            `the value of the most valuable tool or item of plant or equipment`        IS `their most valuable tool is worth`
            `the term of the arrangement in months`                                    IS `the arrangement lasts this many months`
            `more than 1 vehicle is owned or operated for work at the same time`       IS `they run more than 1 vehicle for work at once`
            `the goods are or were owned by the driver or by the other person`         IS `the goods are or were theirs or mine`
            `the vehicle is supplied by the other person or someone related to it`     IS `I or someone related supply their vehicle`
            `a fishing crew member paid by a share of profits or gross receipts`       IS `they are fishing crew paid by a share`
            `a volunteer of whom the Crown is the presumptive employer under Schedule 1` IS `they are a volunteer of a prescribed class`
            `the Corporation has extended the Act's protection to the person under s 175` IS `the Corporation has extended cover to them`
            `the regulation 6 class`                                                   IS `their regulation 6 class`)
        (`CPI figures` WITH
            `the CPI for the September quarter before the adjustment` IS `the CPI for the latest September quarter`
            `the CPI for the base September quarter`                 IS `the CPI for the September quarter of 2014`)

@export I contracted a business to do work I undertook: am I taken to be the employer of its workers (s 4(4), reg 5(8))?
GIVEN `I contracted the contractor for work I took on` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you contracted the contractor to do work that you had undertaken
      `the contractor is registered as an employer under the Act` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the contractor is registered as an employer with ReturnToWorkSA
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Am I taken to be the employer of my contractor's workers` IF
    `the principal is taken to be the employer of the contractor's workers` `I contracted the contractor for work I took on` `the contractor is registered as an employer under the Act`

@export Does this worker's injury arise from employment with me, so that the Act applies to it (s 7)?
GIVEN `the injury is` IS A `Kind of injury` @desc Whether the injury is a physical injury, or a psychiatric injury (pure mental harm)
      `it happened out of or in the course of their work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury arose out of, or in the course of, the employment
      `their work was a significant contributing cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment was a significant contributing cause of the injury (physical injury)
      `their work was the significant contributing cause` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the employment was the significant contributing cause of the injury (psychiatric injury)
      `it came mainly from my reasonable management action` IS A BOOLEAN @desc For a psychiatric injury: whether it arose wholly or predominantly from your reasonable action, taken reasonably, to transfer, demote, discipline, counsel, retrench or dismiss, a reasonable decision not to promote or give a benefit, reasonable administrative action, or reasonable action under the Act
      `it happened at a social or sporting activity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury arose from the worker's involvement in a social or sporting activity
      `the activity was part of their job or I asked them to go` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the activity was part of the employment, or undertaken at your direction or request
      `it happened on a journey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury arose on a journey
      `the journey was part of their duties` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the journey was undertaken in the course of the worker's duties
      `the journey was between home or work and a listed place` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the journey was between the worker's residence and place of employment, or between either and a place of required training, medical services, return to work services or a compensation claim
      `they took a reasonably direct route` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker took a reasonably direct route without a substantial deviation that materially increased the risk
      `there is a real and substantial connection between the job and the journey` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there was a real and substantial connection between the employment and the journey at the time of the accident
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this injury a work injury in my employment` IF
    `the injury arises from employment`
        (`Injury facts` WITH
            `the kind of injury`                                                     IS `the injury is`
            `it arose out of or in the course of employment`                         IS `it happened out of or in the course of their work`
            `employment was a significant contributing cause`                        IS `their work was a significant contributing cause`
            `employment was the significant contributing cause`                      IS `their work was the significant contributing cause`
            `it arose wholly or predominantly from reasonable action or decisions of the kinds in s 7(4)` IS `it came mainly from my reasonable management action`
            `it arose from a social or sporting activity`                            IS `it happened at a social or sporting activity`
            `the activity was part of the employment or at the employer's direction or request` IS `the activity was part of their job or I asked them to go`
            `it arose on a journey`                                                  IS `it happened on a journey`
            `the journey was in the course of carrying out duties of employment`     IS `the journey was part of their duties`
            `the journey was between places listed in s 7(8)(b)`                     IS `the journey was between home or work and a listed place`
            `the route was reasonably direct without a substantial, riskier deviation` IS `they took a reasonably direct route`
            `there is a real and substantial connection between the employment and the journey` IS `there is a real and substantial connection between the job and the journey`)

§§ `Notices and claims I receive (ss 16, 30; reg 11)`

@export Is a notice of injury given this way taken to have been given to me (s 16(4), reg 11)?
GIVEN `how it was given` IS A `Manner of giving notice` @desc How the worker gave notice: to you at your place of business; to the worker's supervisor at the time; to a person you designated; by post to you; by email to an address you use for your business; or some other way
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this notice taken to have been given to me` IF
    `notice given this way is taken to have been given to the employer` `how it was given`

@export By when must I send ReturnToWorkSA a copy of a notice of injury I received (s 16(6))?
GIVEN `the day I received the notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the notice of injury (ISO 8601)
      `weekday public holidays in the next 5 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many South Australian public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the week or so after that day
      `I am a self-insured employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered with ReturnToWorkSA as a self-insured employer
GIVETH A `Forwarding answer`
DECIDE `By when must I send a copy of the notice of injury` IS
    `the employer's 5 business days after receiving it on` `the day I received the notice` `with public holidays` `weekday public holidays in the next 5 business days` `self-insured` `I am a self-insured employer`

@export By when must I forward this worker's claim, with a statement in the designated form, to ReturnToWorkSA (s 30(4), (5))?
GIVEN `the worker was employed by me when the incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was in employment when the incapacity for work began (otherwise the claim goes to ReturnToWorkSA, not to you)
      `the day I received the claim` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the claim (ISO 8601)
      `weekday public holidays in the next 5 business days` IS A NUMBER @desc How many South Australian public holidays fall on a Monday to Friday in the week or so after that day
      `I am a self-insured employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered with ReturnToWorkSA as a self-insured employer
GIVETH A `Forwarding answer`
DECIDE `By when must I forward this claim` IS
    CONSIDER `to whom the claim must be given` `the worker was employed by me when the incapacity began`
    WHEN `the employer` THEN `the employer's 5 business days after receiving it on` `the day I received the claim` `with public holidays` `weekday public holidays in the next 5 business days` `self-insured` `I am a self-insured employer`
    WHEN `the Corporation, not the employer` THEN `no duty to forward: the claim is given to the Corporation, not the employer`

@export What is the most I can be fined for not sending a notice of injury, forwarding a claim, or giving ReturnToWorkSA information it requires (ss 16(6), 30(5), 30(6))?
GIVEN `I am a self-insured employer` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you are registered with ReturnToWorkSA as a self-insured employer (these offences do not apply to a self-insured employer)
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `What is the most I can be fined for each failure` IS
    IF `I am a self-insured employer` THEN 0 ELSE `the maximum penalty under ss 16(6), 30(5) and 30(6)`

§§ `Giving an injured worker suitable work (s 18)`

-- Situation: a worker injured in your employment can now return to work.
@export Must I provide suitable work to this injured worker (s 18(1), (2))?
GIVEN `the worker was incapacitated by a work injury in my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was incapacitated for work by a work injury arising from employment with you (you are the pre-injury employer)
      `the worker is able to return to work` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker is now able to return to work, full-time or part-time, in the old job or another (including because no longer incapacitated)
      `I can establish it is not reasonably practicable` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can establish that it is not reasonably practicable to provide suitable employment (the onus is on you)
      `the worker left me before the incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker had left your employment before the incapacity began
      `the worker resigned after the incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker ended the employment after the incapacity began
      `I can establish a proper dismissal for serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can establish that the worker's employment was properly terminated for serious and wilful misconduct (the onus is on you)
      `the worker agreed to other employment options` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker agreed to new or other employment options under s 25(10a)
      `the worker has returned to work elsewhere or with me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker has otherwise returned to work with you or another employer
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I provide suitable work` IF
    `the pre-injury employer must provide suitable employment`
        (`Suitable work facts` WITH
            `the worker was incapacitated for work by a work injury from this employment` IS `the worker was incapacitated by a work injury in my employment`
            `the worker is able to return to work`                                    IS `the worker is able to return to work`
            `the employer has established it is not reasonably practicable`           IS `I can establish it is not reasonably practicable`
            `the worker left this employer before the incapacity began`               IS `the worker left me before the incapacity began`
            `the worker ended the employment after the incapacity began`              IS `the worker resigned after the incapacity began`
            `the employer has established a proper termination for serious and wilful misconduct` IS `I can establish a proper dismissal for serious and wilful misconduct`
            `the worker agreed to other employment options under s 25(10a)`           IS `the worker agreed to other employment options`
            `the worker has otherwise returned to work`                               IS `the worker has returned to work elsewhere or with me`)

@export By when must I tell the worker in writing whether I will provide suitable work, after receiving their subsection (3) notice (s 18(4b))?
GIVEN `the day I received the worker's notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's subsection (3) notice (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I reply to the worker's notice` IS
    `the last day for the employer's written reply to a notice received on` `the day I received the worker's notice`

@export Until when can the worker apply to the Tribunal for an order that I provide work (s 18(4d), (4e))?
GIVEN `the day I received the worker's notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you received the worker's subsection (3) notice (ISO 8601)
      `I replied in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you gave the worker your written reply
      `the day of my reply` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave your written reply (ISO 8601; any date if you have not replied)
      `the worker had ceased to be incapacitated when giving the notice` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was no longer incapacitated for work by the injury when giving the notice
      `the day the worker ceased to be incapacitated` IS A DATE @desc The day the worker ceased to be incapacitated (ISO 8601; any date if not)
GIVETH A `Tribunal window answer`
DECIDE `Until when can the worker apply to the Tribunal for work` IS
    `the s 18(4d) window for`
        (`Subsection (3) timing facts` WITH
            `the day the employer received the subsection (3) notice`            IS `the day I received the worker's notice`
            `the employer gave a written reply`                                  IS `I replied in writing`
            `the day of the employer's written reply`                            IS `the day of my reply`
            `the worker had ceased to be incapacitated when giving the notice`   IS `the worker had ceased to be incapacitated when giving the notice`
            `the day the worker ceased to be incapacitated`                      IS `the day the worker ceased to be incapacitated`)

§§ `Ending an injured worker's employment (s 20)`

-- Situation: you propose to end the employment of a worker injured in your employment.
@export Must I give the worker and ReturnToWorkSA 28 days notice before ending this worker's employment (s 20)?
GIVEN `the worker's injury arose in my employment` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker suffered a work injury arising from employment with you
      `I can establish serious and wilful misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether you can establish that the employment is properly ended for serious and wilful misconduct (the burden is on you)
      `the worker is in a return to work plan or getting compensation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker is participating in a recovery/return to work plan, or receiving compensation, for the injury
      `the worker's rights are exhausted or the time to claim has passed` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker's rights to compensation for the injury are exhausted, or the time for making a claim has expired
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Must I give notice before ending this worker's employment` IF
    `s 20 notice is required before terminating`
        (`Termination facts` WITH
            `the worker suffered a work injury in this employment`               IS `the worker's injury arose in my employment`
            `a proper termination for serious and wilful misconduct, established by the employer` IS `I can establish serious and wilful misconduct`
            `the worker is in a recovery/return to work plan or receiving compensation for the injury` IS `the worker is in a return to work plan or getting compensation`
            `the worker's rights to compensation are exhausted or the time to claim has expired` IS `the worker's rights are exhausted or the time to claim has passed`)

@export If I give notice of a proposed termination, what is the earliest day the worker's employment may end (s 20(1))?
GIVEN `the day I gave notice` IS A DATE @desc The day you gave the worker and ReturnToWorkSA notice of the proposed termination (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `What is the earliest day I may end the employment` IS
    `the earliest day the employment may end after notice on` `the day I gave notice`

§§ `This worker's benefits, and my exposure to damages (ss 21, 39, 44, 72, 100)`

@export Is this worker a seriously injured worker (s 21)?
GIVEN `their whole person impairment from physical injury` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's degree of whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent, as assessed under s 22 (0 if none)
      `their whole person impairment from psychiatric injury` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's degree of whole person impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent, assessed separately (0 if none)
      `their final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accredited medical practitioner's final examination was on or after the designated day under the 2022 amending Act
      `ReturnToWorkSA has made an interim decision for them` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether ReturnToWorkSA has made an interim decision, still in effect, that the worker is taken to be a seriously injured worker
GIVETH A `Seriously injured answer`
DECIDE `Is this worker a seriously injured worker` IS
    `the s 21 answer for`
        (`Impairment facts` WITH
            `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent`     IS `their whole person impairment from physical injury`
            `the whole person impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent`  IS `their whole person impairment from psychiatric injury`
            `the final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`     IS `their final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`)
        `with an interim decision` `ReturnToWorkSA has made an interim decision for them`

@export Until what day can this worker be paid weekly payments (ss 39(3), 41, 44)?
GIVEN `the worker is a seriously injured worker` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker is a seriously injured worker
      `the first day of their incapacity` IS A DATE @desc The first day for which the worker was entitled to weekly payments (ISO 8601)
      `their date of birth` IS A DATE @desc The worker's date of birth (ISO 8601)
      `the job has a normal retiring age` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether there is a normal retiring age for workers in this kind of employment
      `that retiring age in months` IS A NUMBER @desc That normal retiring age, in months; 0 if none
      `their age pension age in months` IS A NUMBER @desc The age, in months, at which the worker would be eligible for the age pension under the Social Security Act 1991 (Cth)
      `they were still employed when the incapacity began` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker was still in employment when the incapacity first began
GIVETH A `Retiring age answer`
DECIDE `Until when can this worker get weekly payments` IS
    `the last day of weekly payments for`
        (`Retiring age facts` WITH
            `the date of birth`                                           IS `their date of birth`
            `there is a normal retiring age for the kind of employment`   IS `the job has a normal retiring age`
            `the normal retiring age, in months`                          IS `that retiring age in months`
            `the age pension age, in months`                              IS `their age pension age in months`
            `the day incapacity first occurred`                           IS `the first day of their incapacity`
            `still in employment when the incapacity first occurred`      IS `they were still employed when the incapacity began`)
        `if seriously injured` `the worker is a seriously injured worker`

@export Can damages be awarded against me for this worker's injury (s 72)?
GIVEN `their whole person impairment from physical injury` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's degree of permanent impairment from physical injury, in per cent (0 if none)
      `their whole person impairment from psychiatric injury` IS A NUMBER @desc The worker's degree of permanent impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent, assessed separately (0 if none)
      `their final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the accredited medical practitioner's final examination was on or after the designated day under the 2022 amending Act
      `the worker died of the injury` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the worker died as a result of the injury
GIVETH A `Damages answer`
DECIDE `Can damages be awarded against me` IS
    `the s 72 answer for`
        (`Impairment facts` WITH
            `the whole person impairment from physical injury, in per cent`     IS `their whole person impairment from physical injury`
            `the whole person impairment from psychiatric injury, in per cent`  IS `their whole person impairment from psychiatric injury`
            `the final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`     IS `their final examination was on or after the 2022 designated day`)
        `with death` `the worker died of the injury`

@export By when must I apply to the Tribunal for review of a decision about this worker's claim (s 99(2)(b), s 100(1))?
GIVEN `the day I received notice of the decision` IS A DATE @desc The day you received notice of the reviewable decision (ISO 8601)
GIVETH A DATE
DECIDE `By when must I apply to the Tribunal for review` IS
    `the last day to apply to the Tribunal after notice received on` `the day I received notice of the decision`
